{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["The sense of <b>But YHWH was wrathful with me for your sakes</b> — He repeated in this place, meaning: me He commanded at that time to teach you the commandments, that you may do them in the land that you are passing into, and now take from the mouth of Torah, for I am dying in this land and will not be able to teach them to you in the land, and do not forget there what I taught you and not what you saw at Sinai. And by way of truth, it says: Take heed to yourselves exceedingly, lest you corrupt yourselves — for HaShem was wrathful with me out of anxiety concerning this matter, lest you forget the covenant of HaShem your Elohim in the devouring fire at the top of the mountain and make a likeness of anything, and this is the sense of which YHWH your Elohim commanded you. This has already been hinted at in the portion of Ḥukkat ha-Torah. And Rashi wrote: which YHWH your Elohim commanded you — that you shall not make. And this is the plain sense of the verse, and the enlightened will understand these verses in their truth. And the sense of for YHWH your Elohim is a devouring fire — as you saw at the top of the mountain, and the intention is that this is the attribute of justice that is zealous concerning idolatry, and from this verse you will understand every occurrence of <b>YHWH your Elohim</b> mentioned throughout the Torah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "בע\"ז is an abbreviation for בעבודת זרה (concerning idolatry)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:13:53.628038765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}